# gcloud — real-world examples

Google Cloud SDK supports two authorization methods. User account auth is
recommended for a script or automation on a single machine. Service account
auth is recommended for automation deployed across machines in production,
or on a Compute Engine VM where all users have root.

## Authenticate with a service account key

```sh
gcloud auth activate-service-account --key-file [KEY_FILE]
```

## First-time setup and identity checks

```sh
gcloud init          # configure project, region, account
gcloud auth list     # which accounts are active
gcloud config list   # current project/region settings
gcloud info          # SDK environment details
```

## Interactive shell with auto-prompting for flags and inline help

```sh
gcloud components list
gcloud components install alpha
gcloud alpha interactive     # exit with `exit` or Ctrl+q
```

## Compute: find an instance by name

```sh
gcloud compute instances list --filter=name:instance1
```

## Get help on any command

```sh
gcloud help compute instances create
```

## SSH into an instance from the homelab workstation

```sh
gcloud compute ssh david@instance1 --zone us-central1-a
```

## Copy a backup up to a bucket (gsutil ships with the SDK)

```sh
gsutil cp /srv/backups/homelab-$(date +%F).tar.gz gs://my-backup-bucket/
gsutil ls -lh gs://my-backup-bucket/
```

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| gcloud init | initial setup wizard |
| gcloud auth list | show credentialed accounts |
| gcloud config list | show active configuration |
| gcloud components list | show installed SDK components |
| gsutil | Cloud Storage operations |
